    "effect": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Effect",
      "value": "<p>In combat, your regular actions, i.e. your standard, move&nbsp;and quick action, are no longer limited to when it is your&nbsp;turn in the initiative order. You can take them any time</p>\n<p>you like during a round. Make sure to keep track of the&nbsp;actions you have taken during a given round, for example by flipping a card. When you take a regular action&nbsp;in response to what an ally or enemy does, your action&nbsp;resolves after theirs.</p>\n<p>This does not affect other combat rules. You still roll&nbsp;initiative, roll saves at the end of your turn, and use&nbsp;interrupt actions, intercepts and opportunity attacks&nbsp;normally, without any changes.</p>"
    },
